  "notes": "PAIR: {授|さず}ける（{他動詞|たどうし}）= to bestow ↔ {授|さず}かる（{自動詞|じどうし}）= to be granted, to receive\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {賞|しょう}を{授|さず}ける: to bestow an award\n- {称号|しょうごう}を{授|さず}ける: to confer a title\n- {知恵|ちえ}を{授|さず}ける: to impart wisdom\n- {技|わざ}を{授|さず}ける: to teach a technique\n- {命|いのち}を{授|さず}ける: to grant life\n\nUSAGE: A formal, elevated word implying a top-down relationship (superior to subordinate, teacher to student, deity to human). More dignified than あげる or {教|おし}える.",
